5:32:02 PM [express] POST /api/recipes/generate 200 in 35134ms :: [{"title":"Cheesy Veggie Pasta & Egg Muffins","ingredients":["1 cup (about 60g dry) cooked short pasta (e.g., macaroni, rotini)","3 large eggs","1/4 cup (60ml) milk","1 tablespoon (10g) maida (all-purpose flour)","1/2 cup mixed chopped vegetables (e.g., bell peppers, spinach, onion)","1/4 cup (25g) shredded low-fat cheese (e.g., mozzarella, cheddar)","1 teaspoon olive oil","Salt and black pepper to taste","Optional: pinch of garlic powder, dried herbs"],"instructions":"1. Preheat oven to 375°F (190°C) and lightly grease a 6-cup muffin tin.\n2. In a small pan, heat olive oil over medium heat. Sauté the chopped mixed vegetables for 3-5 minutes until tender-crisp. Set aside to cool slightly.\n3. In a large bowl, whisk together eggs, milk, maida, salt, pepper, and optional herbs/garlic powder until well combined.\n4. Stir in the cooked pasta, sautéed vegetables, and shredded cheese into the egg mixture.\n5. Divide the mixture evenly among the prepared muffin cups, filling each about 3/4 full.\n6. Bake for 18-22 minutes, or until the muffins are golden brown and a toothpick inserted into the center comes out clean.\n7. Let cool in the muffin tin for a few minutes before removing. Serve warm.","macros":{"calories":465,"protein":27,"carbs":36,"fats":21}},{"title":"Savory Spinach & Egg Crepes","ingredients":["1/2 cup (60g) maida (all-purpose flour) (or whole wheat flour for a healthier option)","1/2 cup (120ml) milk","1 large egg (for batter)","1/4 teaspoon salt (for batter)","1 teaspoon olive oil (for cooking crepes)","2 large eggs (for filling)","2 cups (approx. 100g) fresh spinach","1 small clove garlic, minced","1/4 small onion, finely chopped","1 tablespoon milk (for filling, optional, for creaminess)","Salt and pepper to taste (for filling)"],"instructions":"1. **Prepare the Crepe Batter:** In a bowl, whisk together maida, 1/2 cup milk, 1 large egg, and 1/4 teaspoon salt until smooth. Let the batter rest for 10-15 minutes.\n2. **Cook the Crepes:** Heat a non-stick pan or crepe maker over medium heat. Lightly grease with a tiny bit of olive oil. Pour about 1/4 cup of batter into the pan, tilting to spread it thinly and evenly. Cook for 1-2 minutes per side until golden. Repeat for remaining batter (should yield 2-3 crepes).\n3. **Prepare the Filling:** In the same pan, heat 1/2 teaspoon olive oil. Sauté chopped onion and minced garlic for 1-2 minutes until fragrant. Add spinach and cook until wilted, squeezing out excess water if necessary.\n4. In a separate bowl, whisk the 2 filling eggs with 1 tablespoon milk (if using), salt, and pepper. Pour into the pan with the spinach mixture and scramble until cooked through.\n5. **Assemble:** Lay a crepe flat, spoon a portion of the spinach and scrambled egg filling down the center, and fold or roll the crepe. Serve immediately.","macros":{"calories":565,"protein":32,"carbs":55,"fats":23}},{"title":"Lemony Creamy Egg & Tomato Pasta","ingredients":["2 oz (60g) dry pasta (e.g., spaghetti, linguine)","1 large egg yolk","1/4 cup (60ml) milk","1 teaspoon (3g) maida (all-purpose flour)","1/2 cup cherry tomatoes, halved","1 clove garlic, minced","1/2 cup fresh spinach","1 tablespoon grated Parmesan cheese (optional, but recommended)","1 teaspoon olive oil","Zest of 1/2 lemon","Salt and black pepper to taste","Reserved pasta water (approx. 1/4 cup)"],"instructions":"1. Cook pasta according to package directions. Before draining, reserve about 1/2 cup of pasta water. Drain the pasta.\n2. In a small bowl, whisk together the egg yolk, milk, maida, and Parmesan cheese (if using) until smooth. Set aside.\n3. In a large pan or skillet, heat olive oil over medium heat. Add minced garlic and sauté for 30 seconds until fragrant. Add halved cherry tomatoes and cook for 3-4 minutes until they begin to soften.\n4. Stir in the fresh spinach and cook until wilted.\n5. Reduce heat to low. Add the cooked pasta to the pan. Gradually pour in the egg yolk mixture, tossing constantly with tongs to coat the pasta. Add reserved pasta water a tablespoon at a time until a creamy sauce forms. Ensure the heat is low to prevent the egg from scrambling.\n6. Stir in the lemon zest. Season with salt and pepper to taste. Serve immediately.","macros":{"calories":365,"protein":15,"carbs":51,"fats":12}},{"title":"Hearty Baked Egg & Pasta Casserole","ingredients":["1.5 cups (approx. 90g dry) cooked short pasta (e.g., penne, fusilli)","3 large eggs","1/2 cup (120ml) milk","1 tablespoon (10g) maida (all-purpose flour)","1 cup mixed chopped vegetables (e.g., broccoli florets, diced carrots, peas)","1/4 cup (25g) shredded low-fat cheese","1 tablespoon chopped fresh parsley or chives","1 teaspoon olive oil","Salt and black pepper to taste"],"instructions":"1. Preheat oven to 375°F (190°C). Lightly grease an 8x8 inch baking dish.\n2. In a large bowl, whisk together eggs, milk, maida, salt, and pepper until well combined and smooth.\n3. In a separate bowl, toss the cooked pasta with chopped mixed vegetables. For quicker cooking, you can lightly steam or sauté the harder vegetables (like carrots or broccoli) for 2-3 minutes beforehand.\n4. Add the pasta and vegetable mixture to the egg and milk mixture. Stir in the fresh herbs.\n5. Pour the entire mixture into the prepared baking dish. Sprinkle the shredded cheese evenly over the top.\n6. Bake for 25-35 minutes, or until the casserole is set in the center and golden brown on top. Let it rest for a few minutes before serving.","macros":{"calories":565,"protein":31,"carbs":57,"fats":22}},{"title":"Nourishing Creamy Egg Drop Pasta Soup","ingredients":["1.5 oz (40g) dry small pasta (e.g., orzo, stelline, or broken spaghetti)","1 large egg","1/4 cup (60ml) milk","1 teaspoon (3g) maida (all-purpose flour)","3 cups (720ml) low-sodium vegetable broth","1/2 cup mixed finely diced vegetables (e.g., carrots, celery, peas)","1 teaspoon olive oil","Salt and black pepper to taste","Optional: fresh parsley for garnish"],"instructions":"1. In a medium pot, heat olive oil over medium heat. Add the finely diced vegetables and sauté for 3-4 minutes until slightly softened.\n2. In a small bowl, whisk together the maida with a tablespoon or two of milk to form a slurry, then mix in the remaining milk and the egg until well combined.\n3. Pour the vegetable broth into the pot with the sautéed vegetables and bring to a simmer. Add the pasta and cook according to package directions until al dente.\n4. Once the pasta is cooked, reduce the heat to low. Slowly drizzle the egg and milk mixture into the simmering soup in a thin stream, stirring constantly with a fork or whisk to create delicate egg ribbons.\n5. Continue stirring gently for about 1 minute until the egg is cooked through. Do not boil vigorously after adding the egg.\n6. Season the soup with salt and pepper to taste. Ladle into bowls and garnish with fresh parsley if desired. Serve warm.","macros":{"calories":335,"protein":15,"carbs":41,"fats":12}}]
5:32:20 PM [express] POST /api/recipes 201 in 53ms :: {"id":2,"userId":"53172143","title":"Cheesy Veggie Pasta & Egg Muffins","ingredients":["1 cup (about 60g dry) cooked short pasta (e.g., macaroni, rotini)","3 large eggs","1/4 cup (60ml) milk","1 tablespoon (10g) maida (all-purpose flour)","1/2 cup mixed chopped vegetables (e.g., bell peppers, spinach, onion)","1/4 cup (25g) shredded low-fat cheese (e.g., mozzarella, cheddar)","1 teaspoon olive oil","Salt and black pepper to taste","Optional: pinch of garlic powder, dried herbs"],"instructions":"1. Preheat oven to 375°F (190°C) and lightly grease a 6-cup muffin tin.\n2. In a small pan, heat olive oil over medium heat. Sauté the chopped mixed vegetables for 3-5 minutes until tender-crisp. Set aside to cool slightly.\n3. In a large bowl, whisk together eggs, milk, maida, salt, pepper, and optional herbs/garlic powder until well combined.\n4. Stir in the cooked pasta, sautéed vegetables, and shredded cheese into the egg mixture.\n5. Divide the mixture evenly among the prepared muffin cups, filling each about 3/4 full.\n6. Bake for 18-22 minutes, or until the muffins are golden brown and a toothpick inserted into the center comes out clean.\n7. Let cool in the muffin tin for a few minutes before removing. Serve warm.","macros":{"fats":21,"carbs":36,"protein":27,"calories":465},"isSaved":true,"createdAt":"2026-03-19T17:32:20.554Z"}
5:32:20 PM [express] GET /api/recipes 200 in 7ms :: [{"id":2,"userId":"53172143","title":"Cheesy Veggie Pasta & Egg Muffins","ingredients":["1 cup (about 60g dry) cooked short pasta (e.g., macaroni, rotini)","3 large eggs","1/4 cup (60ml) milk","1 tablespoon (10g) maida (all-purpose flour)","1/2 cup mixed chopped vegetables (e.g., bell peppers, spinach, onion)","1/4 cup (25g) shredded low-fat cheese (e.g., mozzarella, cheddar)","1 teaspoon olive oil","Salt and black pepper to taste","Optional: pinch of garlic powder, dried herbs"],"instructions":"1. Preheat oven to 375°F (190°C) and lightly grease a 6-cup muffin tin.\n2. In a small pan, heat olive oil over medium heat. Sauté the chopped mixed vegetables for 3-5 minutes until tender-crisp. Set aside to cool slightly.\n3. In a large bowl, whisk together eggs, milk, maida, salt, pepper, and optional herbs/garlic powder until well combined.\n4. Stir in the cooked pasta, sautéed vegetables, and shredded cheese into the egg mixture.\n5. Divide the mixture evenly among the prepared muffin cups, filling each about 3/4 full.\n6. Bake for 18-22 minutes, or until the muffins are golden brown and a toothpick inserted into the center comes out clean.\n7. Let cool in the muffin tin for a few minutes before removing. Serve warm.","macros":{"fats":21,"carbs":36,"protein":27,"calories":465},"isSaved":true,"createdAt":"2026-03-19T17:32:20.554Z"}]
